{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q409309","formula":"CH₄S","hill":"CH4S","elements":["H","C","S"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"H":4.0,"S":1.0},"names":{"en":"Methyl mercaptan","ru":"Метантиол"},"descriptions":{"en":"Methanethiol ( METH-ayn-THY-ol), also called methyl mercaptan, is an organosulfur compound with the chemical formula CH3SH. It is a colorless flammable gas with a distinctive putrid smell. In small amounts, it is pervasive in nature and found in certain foods, such as some nuts and cheese. It contributes to many odors, including the emissions from pulp mills, bad breath, and flatus.","ru":"Метантио́л (метилмеркапта́н) CH3SH — простейший представитель гомологического ряда тиолов, бесцветный токсичный газ с сильным неприятным запахом, при малых концентрациях напоминающим запах гнилой капусты."},"fame":38,"pubchemCid":878,"mass":48.11,"charge":0,"smiles":"CS","inchikey":"LSDPWZHWYPCBBB-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"methanethiol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"878","atoms":6,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.902,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"S"},{"x":-0.902,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.274,"y":1.01,"z":0.19,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.274,"y":-0.669,"z":0.78,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.273,"y":-0.341,"z":-0.97,"el":"H"},{"x":1.055,"y":0.442,"z":1.257,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1],[0,5,1],[1,2,1],[1,3,1],[1,4,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q409309","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Methanethiol","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9C%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B0%D0%BD%D1%82%D0%B8%D0%BE%D0%BB","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"properties","name":"PubChem","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih